          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            inherits the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            under pointwise group multiplication of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loops"} loops
            %em loop group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            (Notice that this is a group structure in addition to the
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-group"} infinity-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
            under
            %em composition
            of loops.)
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \to G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+structure+of+mapping+spaces"} manifold structure of mapping spaces
            the collection of such smooth maps is itself an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+smooth+manifold"} infinite-dimensional smooth manifold
            and so the smooth loop group of a Lie group is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+Lie+group"} infinite-dimensional Lie group
          %p
            Among all
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinite-dimensional+Lie+groups"} infinite-dimensional Lie groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            is similar to that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
          %p
            Some of these nice properties are solely due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            being a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+manifold"} compact manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            any other compact manifold there is similarly an infinite-dimensional Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,G]
            of smooth functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to G
            under pointwise multiplication in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Such mapping groups appear in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            notably as groups of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformations"} gauge transformations
            over a
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            describing the propagation of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/current+algebras"} current algebras
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+algebras"}> affine algebras
            ) which arise as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"}> centrally extended
            ) loop groups derive their name from this relation to physics. Accordingly, as for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+groups"} compact Lie groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            of loop groups is naturally understood in terms of their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            (by a loop variant of the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
          %p
            On the other hand, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            greater that 1 there are very few known results about the properties of the mapping group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [X,G]
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#lie_algebra Lie algebra
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G
              is the
              %span.newWikiWord
                loop Lie algebra
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/loop+Lie+algebra"} ?
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi L
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi L
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Lie(L G) \simeq L Lie(G) = L \mathfrak{g}
                    \\,.
          %h3#complexification Complexification
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %span.newWikiWord
                complexification
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/complexification+of+a+Lie+group"} ?
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G
              is the loop group of the complexification of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L G)_{\mathbb{C}}
                    \\simeq
                    L (G_\mathbb{C})
                    \\,.
          %h3#central_extensions Central extensions
          %p
            Loop groups of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groups"} Lie groups
            have canonical
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
            %em Kac-Moody central extensions
            \. A detailed discussion is in (
            %a{:href => "#PressleySegal"}> Pressley &amp; Segal
            ). A review is in (
            %a{:href => "#BCSS"}> BCSS
            )
          %h3#Representations Representations
          %h4#positive_energy Positive energy
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi t
                    %mi θ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi L
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mi L
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  t_\theta \colon L G \to L G
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
            which rotates loops by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angle"} angle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
          %p
            The corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product+group"} semidirect product group
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mi G
                  %mo ⋊
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G \rtimes S^1
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+space"} topological vector space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S^1 \to Aut(V)
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              is called
              %strong positive
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i \theta)
              acts by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi A
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(i A \theta)
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in End(V)
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
              with positive
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum+of+an+operator"} spectrum
            %p
              A linear
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho : L G \to Aut(V)
            %p
              is said to have
              %strong positive energy
              or to be a
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+representation"} positive energy representation
              if it extends to a representation of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semidirect+product+group"} semidirect product group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⋊
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G \rtimes S^1
              such that the restriction to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              is positive.
          %h4#ByGeometricQuantization By geometric quantization (looped orbit method)
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+loop+groups"} quantization of loop groups
            in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            of their canonical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+bundle"} prequantum bundle
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Lie+group"} compact Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \hookrightarrow G
            be the inclusion of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+torus"} maximal torus
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+sequence"} fiber sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi T
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi L
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi T
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi L
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  G/T &amp;\to&amp; L G / T
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; L G / G &amp; \simeq \Omega G
                  }
                  \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              By the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+group"} semisimple Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/T
              is isomorphic to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbit"} coadjoint orbit
              of an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \lambda , -\rangle \in \mathfrak{g}^*
              for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T \simeq G_\lambda
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stabilizer+subgroup"} stabilizer subgroup
            %p
              If moreover
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+lattice"} weight lattice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi wt
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔱
                      %mo *
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝔱
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{wt} \subset \mathfrak{t}^* \simeq \mathfrak{t}
              of the Lie group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to the group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+characters"} group characters
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mi wt
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi LieGrp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{wt} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Hom_{LieGrp}(G,U(1))
                    \\,.
          #RepsFromGeometricQuantization.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+representation"} projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+energy+representations"} positive energy representations
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G
              correspond precisley to the possible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantizations"} geometric quantizations
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G / T
              (as in the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
            %p More in detail:
            %p
              The degree-2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G / T
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi T
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^2(L G / T) \simeq \mathbb{Z} \oplus H^2(G / T, \mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z} \oplus \hat T
                    \\,.
            %p
              Writing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{n,\lambda}
              for the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+line+bundle"} complex line bundle
              with level
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
              and weight
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \in \hat T
              we have that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the space of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+sections"} holomorphic sections
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi L
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mi λ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_{n,\lambda}
                  is either zero or is an irreducible positive energy representation;
              %li
                %p every such arises this way;
              %li
                %p
                  and is non-zero precisely if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,\lambda)
                  is positive in the sense that for each positive
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    coroot
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/coroot"} ?
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi α
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_\alpha
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi λ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi α
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        0 \leq \lambda(h_\alpha) \leq n \langle h_\alpha, h_\alpha\rangle
                        \\,.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Segal"}> Segal, prop. 4.2
            ).
          %h3#RelationToEquivariantEllipticCohomology Relation to equivariant elliptic cohomology
          %p
            Under mild conditions (but over the complex numbers) the representation ring of a loop group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L G
            is equivalent to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            (see there for more) of the point (
            %a{:href => "#Ando00"}> Ando 00, theorem 10.10
            ).
          %p
            This is a higher analog of how
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
            of the point gives the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+ring"} representation ring
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Moody+group"} Kac-Moody group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verlinde+ring"} Verlinde ring
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+group"} string group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/caloron+correspondence"} caloron correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac+character+formula"} Kac character formula
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kac-Weyl+character"} Kac-Weyl character
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+loop+group"} double loop group
          %h2#references References
          %p The standard textbook on loop groups is
          %ul
            %li#PressleySegal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Pressley"}> Andrew Pressley
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"} Graeme Segal
              = succeed "," do
                %em Loop groups
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/loop-groups-9780198535614"} ISBN:9780198535614
          %p A review talk is
          %ul
            %li#Segal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              %em Loop groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://people.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/zagier/files/doi/10.1007/BFb0084581/chapter08.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            A review of some aspects with an eye towards loop groups as part of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            of groups representing a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+2-group"} string 2-group
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BCSS05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"}> John Baez
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alissa+Crans"} Alissa Crans
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              = succeed "," do
                %em From loop groups to 2-groups
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0504123"} arXiv:math/0504123
          %p
            The relation between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            of loop groups and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            over the group is the topic of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Freed"}> Dan Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Hopkins"} Mike Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Loop+Groups+and+Twisted+K-Theory"} Loop Groups and Twisted K-Theory
          %p
            The relation between representations of loop groups an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+elliptic+cohomology"} equivariant elliptic cohomology
            of the point is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Ando00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matthew+Ando"}> Matthew Ando
              ,
              %em Power operations in elliptic cohomology and representations of loop groups
              Transactions of the American
              %p
                Mathematical Society 352, 2000, pp. 5619-5666. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/221905"}> JSTOR
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~mando/papers/POECLG/poeclg.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion with respect to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flag+varieties"} flag varieties
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Kumar02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shrawan+Kumar"}> Shrawan Kumar
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Kac-Moody Groups, their Flag Varieties and Representation Theory
